// codebox_pass.gen -- f_wc PARITY hold/reseed stage (spec Revision 2, S6).
// Mirror: wc_parity_mirror.pass_stage().
// Inputs: in1 = the `r draw` bang (unused; it only triggers the render each frame), in2 = the
// feedback state (R = E, G = I, B = contour, A = 1 flag, from nl through hold), in3 = the seed
// stage (all four channels).
//   - reseed >= 0.5 replaces the whole state with the seed (load, reset)
//   - LOST FLAG = alpha: nl always writes A = 1, a fresh or reallocated texture reads A = 0 (to be
//     confirmed at T046). NOT "E == 0 and I == 0": E = I = 0 is a legitimate state under 8-bit
//     quantization, and that old self-heal would inject noise into a live field
//   - the feedback is NaN/Inf-guarded: abs(x) < 1e30 (NaN == NaN is TRUE on this GPU); a zapped
//     channel reads 0 and the texel is held (its alpha is kept)
//   - selection uses switch(), not mix() (mix(NaN, x, 1) is still NaN)
Param reseed(0);

fbe = nearest(in2, norm).x;
fbe = switch(abs(fbe) < 1e30, fbe, 0);
fbi = nearest(in2, norm).y;
fbi = switch(abs(fbi) < 1e30, fbi, 0);
fbb = nearest(in2, norm).z;
fbb = switch(abs(fbb) < 1e30, fbb, 0);
fba = nearest(in2, norm).w;
fba = switch(abs(fba) < 1e30, fba, 0);
sd = nearest(in3, norm);
take = switch(reseed >= 0.5, 1, switch(fba == 0, 1, 0));
out1 = vec(switch(take > 0.5, sd.x, fbe), switch(take > 0.5, sd.y, fbi),
           switch(take > 0.5, sd.z, fbb), switch(take > 0.5, sd.w, fba));
